{"id": "aab0e850-178e-4b2f-a2de-5841465cdc65", "slug": "high-performance-infrastructure-stats", "title": "High-Performance Infrastructure Stats", "description": "High Performance Onboarding Section is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.", "content": "---\nversion: \"neuform-top-creators-featured\"\nname: \"High-Performance Infrastructure Stats\"\ndescription: \"High Performance Onboarding Section is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.\"\ncolors:\n  primary: \"#4AB9FF\"\n  secondary: \"#0B1021\"\n  accent: \"#6496FF\"\n  background: \"#050811\"\n  surface: \"#2A3A5C\"\n  text-primary: \"#FFFFFF\"\n  text-secondary: \"#A1A1AA\"\n  border: \"#27272A\"\ntypography:\n  display-lg:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"64px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: \"1.04\"\n    letterSpacing: \"0\"\n  body-md:\n    fontFamily: \"Inter\"\n    fontSize: \"16px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: \"1.6\"\n  label-md:\n    fontFamily: \"JetBrains Mono\"\n    fontSize: \"12px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    lineHeight: \"1.2\"\nspacing:\n  base: \"8px\"\n  gap: \"16px\"\n  card-padding: \"24px\"\n  section-padding: \"80px\"\nrounded:\n  card: \"8px\"\n  control: \"8px\"\n  pill: \"9999px\"\ncomponents:\n  card:\n    background: \"Use the surface token with subtle borders and HTML-matched shadow depth\"\n    radius: \"Match the declared card radius token\"\n  button:\n    background: \"Use primary or accent colors for the main action\"\n    radius: \"Use the control or pill radius based on the source HTML\"\n---\n# High-Performance Infrastructure Stats\nSource: Neuform Featured templates from top creators. Author: Sourany Phomhome (@sou). Views: 5; favorites: 2; remixes: 1.\nTags: pricing, section, animated, charts, billing, cta.\n## Overview\nHigh Performance Onboarding Section is designed for building reusable UI components in modern web projects. Key features include reusable structure, responsive behavior, and production-ready presentation. It is suitable for component libraries and responsive product interfaces.\n\nBuilt for relentless scale. Process critical workflows with stable throughput, low latency, and resilient performance even during unpredictable demand spikes. 0 M+ automated tasks completed monthly 0 K+ events processed…\n## Composition\nUse the attached HTML reference as the source of truth. Preserve the visible hierarchy, first-screen composition, section rhythm, density, and interaction tone before adapting copy or content.\nKey visible headings include: Built for relentless scale..\n## Colors\nAnchor the palette in primary #4AB9FF, secondary #0B1021, accent #6496FF, background #050811, surface #2A3A5C, text-primary #FFFFFF. Keep background, surface, text, and border roles distinct so generated layouts retain the same contrast pattern as the source.\n## Typography\nUse Inter for display moments and Inter for body copy unless the HTML clearly demands a compatible fallback. Labels and technical metadata should use JetBrains Mono or an equivalent mono face.\n## Layout\nKeep spacing deliberate and stable. Favor the same grid direction, max-width behavior, card density, and responsive stacking seen in the HTML. Do not replace distinctive source structures with generic SaaS sections.\n## Components\nDashboard, chart, and data panels should preserve their compact operational hierarchy, nested surfaces, and metric emphasis.\n## Motion\nPreserve existing motion cues such as masked reveals, staggered entrance, hover lift, scroll-triggered transitions, and ambient movement. Keep easing smooth and restrained.\n## WebGL & Effects\n\nIf the source includes canvas, WebGL, Three.js, gradients, particles, or atmospheric effects, rebuild them as supporting layers behind the content. Keep effects performant, responsive, and secondary to the interface.\n\n## Guardrails\n- Do not flatten the source into a generic card grid.\n- Do not swap the color mode unless the source clearly supports it.\n- Preserve the first viewport signal, focal object, and visual density.\n- Keep buttons, cards, and badges aligned to the same radius and border language.", "preview_html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>High-Performance Infrastructure Stats</title>\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://code.iconify.design/iconify-icon/1.0.7/iconify-icon.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/ScrollTrigger.min.js\"></script>\n    <style>\n        /* Base optimizations and custom utility for text reveal */\n        ::selection { background-color: rgba(168, 85, 247, 0.3); color: white; }\n        .text-reveal-wrap { display: inline-flex; overflow: hidden; vertical-align: bottom; margin-right: 0.25em; padding-bottom: 0.1em; margin-bottom: -0.1em; }\n        .text-reveal-inner { display: inline-block; transform: translateY(110%); will-change: transform; }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body class=\"bg-[#050811] text-slate-200 font-sans antialiased min-h-screen flex items-center justify-center p-4 md:p-12 overflow-x-hidden selection:bg-fuchsia-500/30 selection:text-white\">\n\n    <!-- Main Container -->\n    <section class=\"relative w-full max-w-7xl mx-auto min-h-[650px] md:min-h-[800px] border border-[#1e293b]/80 bg-[#0B1021] overflow-hidden flex flex-col justify-between shadow-2xl shadow-black/80 group\">\n\n        <!-- Subtle Internal Grid Guides -->\n        <div class=\"absolute top-0 inset-x-0 h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-[#2a3a5c] to-transparent opacity-40\"></div>\n        <div class=\"absolute bottom-0 inset-x-0 h-px bg-gradient-to-r from-transparent via-[#2a3a5c] to-transparent opacity-20\"></div>\n\n        <!-- Flowing Neon Wave Canvas -->\n        <canvas id=\"dataWave\" class=\"absolute inset-0 w-full h-full pointer-events-none transition-opacity duration-1000 ease-in-out opacity-90 group-hover:opacity-100\" style=\"z-index: 1;\"></canvas>\n\n        <!-- Top Header Content -->\n        <div class=\"relative z-10 px-6 py-12 md:px-16 md:py-20 max-w-3xl pointer-events-none\">\n            <h2 class=\"js-reveal-text text-3xl lg:text-4xl tracking-tight font-medium text-white mb-4 leading-tight\">\n                Built for relentless scale.\n            </h2>\n            <p class=\"js-reveal-text text-lg lg:text-xl tracking-tight font-normal text-slate-400 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl\">\n                Process critical workflows with stable throughput, low latency, and resilient performance even during unpredictable demand spikes.\n            </p>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Bottom Stats Section -->\n        <div class=\"relative z-10 px-6 py-12 md:px-16 md:py-16 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-10 md:gap-8 border-t border-[#1e293b]/40 bg-gradient-to-t from-[#0B1021] via-[#0B1021]/80 to-transparent mt-auto pointer-events-none\">\n\n            <!-- Metric 1 -->\n            <div class=\"flex flex-col js-stat-reveal opacity-0 translate-y-6\">\n                <div class=\"flex items-baseline gap-1\">\n                    <span class=\"text-6xl lg:text-7xl tracking-tight font-medium text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-[linear-gradient(to_right,#FF8A7A,#FF6B9E)] js-counter\" data-target=\"320\">0</span>\n                    <span class=\"text-5xl lg:text-6xl tracking-tight font-medium text-[#FF6B9E]\">M+</span>\n                </div>\n                <span class=\"text-sm font-normal text-slate-400 mt-3 max-w-[220px] leading-snug\">automated tasks completed monthly</span>\n            </div>\n\n            <!-- Metric 2 -->\n            <div class=\"flex flex-col js-stat-reveal opacity-0 translate-y-6\">\n                <div class=\"flex items-baseline gap-1\">\n                    <span class=\"text-6xl lg:text-7xl tracking-tight font-medium text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-[linear-gradient(to_right,#E178ED,#9B66FF)] js-counter\" data-target=\"18\">0</span>\n                    <span class=\"text-5xl lg:text-6xl tracking-tight font-medium text-[#9B66FF]\">K+</span>\n                </div>\n                <span class=\"text-sm font-normal text-slate-400 mt-3 max-w-[220px] leading-snug\">events processed every second</span>\n            </div>\n\n            <!-- Metric 3 -->\n            <div class=\"flex flex-col js-stat-reveal opacity-0 translate-y-6\">\n                <div class=\"flex items-baseline gap-1\">\n                    <span class=\"text-6xl lg:text-7xl tracking-tight font-medium text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-[linear-gradient(to_right,#748EF5,#4AB9FF)] js-counter\" data-target=\"92\">0</span>\n                    <span class=\"text-5xl lg:text-6xl tracking-tight font-medium text-[#4AB9FF]\">K+</span>\n                </div>\n                <span class=\"text-sm font-normal text-slate-400 mt-3 max-w-[220px] leading-snug\">decisions executed per minute</span>\n            </div>\n\n        </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <script>\n        document.addEventListener(\"DOMContentLoaded\", () => {\n            gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);\n\n            // --- 1. Text Masked Reveal Animation Setup ---\n            const revealTexts = document.querySelectorAll('.js-reveal-text');\n            revealTexts.forEach(el => {\n                const text = el.textContent;\n                el.innerHTML = '';\n                // Split text by whitespace, filtering out empty strings\n                const words = text.split(/\\s+/).filter(w => w.trim().length > 0);\n\n                words.forEach(word => {\n                    const wrap = document.createElement('span');\n                    wrap.className = 'text-reveal-wrap';\n                    const inner = document.createElement('span');\n                    inner.className = 'text-reveal-inner';\n                    inner.textContent = word;\n                    wrap.appendChild(inner);\n                    el.appendChild(wrap);\n                });\n\n                // GSAP ScrollTrigger for the text reveal\n                ScrollTrigger.create({\n                    trigger: el,\n                    start: \"top 90%\",\n                    onEnter: () => {\n                        gsap.to(el.querySelectorAll('.text-reveal-inner'), {\n                            y: \"0%\",\n                            duration: 0.85,\n                            stagger: 0.02,\n                            ease: \"power3.out\"\n                        });\n                    },\n                    once: true\n                });\n            });\n\n            // --- 2. Stats & Counter Animation Setup ---\n            const statBlocks = document.querySelectorAll('.js-stat-reveal');\n            if (statBlocks.length > 0) {\n                ScrollTrigger.create({\n                    trigger: statBlocks[0].parentElement,\n                    start: \"top 95%\",\n                    onEnter: () => {\n                        // Fade and slide up the blocks\n                        gsap.to(statBlocks, {\n                            opacity: 1,\n                            y: 0,\n                            duration: 0.9,\n                            stagger: 0.15,\n                            ease: \"power2.out\"\n                        });\n\n                        // Animate the counters counting up\n                        document.querySelectorAll('.js-counter').forEach((counter, i) => {\n                            const target = parseInt(counter.getAttribute('data-target'), 10);\n                            gsap.to(counter, {\n                                innerHTML: target,\n                                duration: 2.5,\n                                delay: i * 0.15,\n                                ease: \"power3.out\",\n                                snap: { innerHTML: 1 }\n                            });\n                        });\n                    },\n                    once: true\n                });\n            }\n\n            // --- 3. Flowing Neon Canvas Wave ---\n            const canvas = document.getElementById('dataWave');\n            const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n            let width, height;\n\n            // Handle high-DPI displays for crisp rendering\n            function resize() {\n                const dpr = window.devicePixelRatio || 1;\n                width = canvas.parentElement.offsetWidth;\n                height = canvas.parentElement.offsetHeight;\n                canvas.width = width * dpr;\n                canvas.height = height * dpr;\n                ctx.scale(dpr, dpr);\n            }\n            window.addEventListener('resize', resize);\n            resize();\n\n            let time = 0;\n            const numLines = 70;\n            let currentGlow = 0.5;\n            let targetGlow = 0.5;\n\n            // Subtle interaction: increase glow intensity on hover\n            const container = canvas.parentElement;\n            container.addEventListener('mouseenter', () => targetGlow = 0.85);\n            container.addEventListener('mouseleave', () => targetGlow = 0.5);\n\n            function renderWave() {\n                ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height);\n\n                // Smoothly interpolate glow intensity\n                currentGlow += (targetGlow - currentGlow) * 0.05;\n\n                // Screen blending mode creates the overlapping luminous neon effect\n                ctx.globalCompositeOperation = 'screen';\n\n                for (let i = 0; i < numLines; i++) {\n                    ctx.beginPath();\n\n                    // Normalize line index from -1 to 1 for vertical distribution\n                    const normalizedI = (i / numLines) * 2 - 1;\n\n                    // Construct the rich gradient based on the requested palette\n                    const gradient = ctx.createLinearGradient(0, 0, width, 0);\n                    gradient.addColorStop(0, `rgba(255, 110, 199, 0)`);                   // Fade in\n                    gradient.addColorStop(0.2, `rgba(255, 110, 199, ${currentGlow * 0.25})`); // Pink\n                    gradient.addColorStop(0.5, `rgba(190, 80, 255, ${currentGlow * 0.35})`);  // Violet/Magenta\n                    gradient.addColorStop(0.8, `rgba(100, 150, 255, ${currentGlow * 0.25})`); // Electric Blue\n                    gradient.addColorStop(1, `rgba(100, 150, 255, 0)`);                   // Fade out\n\n                    ctx.strokeStyle = gradient;\n                    ctx.lineWidth = 1.2;\n\n                    // Plot the line points\n                    for (let x = 0; x <= width; x += 15) {\n                        const nx = x / width; // Normalized X position (0 to 1)\n\n                        // Exponential spread calculation: creates the pinched-left, fanned-right geometry\n                        const spread = Math.pow(nx, 2.5) * (height * 0.4);\n\n                        const freq = 1.8;\n                        const phase = time * 0.0006;\n\n                        // Create complex overlapping wave motion\n                        const wave1 = Math.sin(nx * Math.PI * freq + phase + normalizedI * 0.6);\n                        const wave2 = Math.cos(nx * Math.PI * (freq * 1.3) - phase * 1.1);\n\n                        // Base vertical center\n                        let y = height * 0.55;\n\n                        // Apply architectural shaping to the wave\n                        y += nx * (height * 0.05); // Slight overall downward drift\n                        y += normalizedI * spread; // Fan out vertically based on line index\n\n                        // Add organic wobbly distortion, scaled by the spread so the origin point remains tight\n                        y += wave1 * spread * 0.35;\n                        y += wave2 * spread * 0.15;\n\n                        if (x === 0) ctx.moveTo(x, y);\n                        else ctx.lineTo(x, y);\n                    }\n                    ctx.stroke();\n                }\n\n                time += 16;\n                requestAnimationFrame(renderWave);\n            }\n\n            // Initiate the render loop\n            renderWave();\n        });\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>", "preview_file_name": "high-performance-infrastructure-stats.html", "thumbnail_url": "https://hoirqrkdgbmvpwutwuwj.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/design-system-thumbnails/regenerated-2026-05-22-2s/high-performance-infrastructure-stats.jpg", "source_name": "high-performance-infrastructure-stats-DESIGN.md", "views": 58, "forks": 5, "private": false, "featured": true, "created_by": "8bd0314a-9525-4a13-996e-2c37cbd9e514", "created_at": "2026-05-01T16:18:09.070118+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-07-03T11:06:59.10439+00:00"}